<h2>Subdomain Modeling in ADCIRC</h2>

<blockquote>
What is it?  An exact reanalysis technique for storm surge and tides
that enables the assessment of local <em>subdomain</em> changes with
less computational effort than would be required by a complete
resimulation of the full domain. So long as the subdomain is large
enough to fully contain the altered hydrodynamics, changes may be made
and simulations performed within it without the need to calculate new
boundary values.

<br><br>

Subdomain modeling is now built into the official
<a href="http://adcirc.org">ADCIRC</a> release, beginning with v51.42
(as of Jan 28, 2015).
</blockquote>


<h4>Subdomain ADCIRC+SWAN v53</h4>

<blockquote>
